.TH "PVVERIFY" "1" "2026-08-11" "s390-tools" "Pvverify Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.SH "NAME"
pvverify \- Tool to verify host\-keys
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.fam C
 \fBpvverify\fR [OPTIONS] \fB\-\-host\-key\-document\fR <FILE> <\-\-no\-verify|\-\-cert <FILE>>
.fam C
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Tool to verify host\-keys. Use this tool to verify the chain of trust for IBM
Secure
.SH "OPTIONS"
\-k, \-\-host\-key\-document <FILE>
.RS 4
Use FILE as a host\-key document.

Can be specified multiple times and must be specified at least once.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-verify
.RS 4
Disable the host\-key document verification.

Does not require the host\-key documents to be valid. Do not use for a
production request unless you verified the host\-key document beforehand.
.RE
.PP
\-C, \-\-cert <FILE>
.RS 4
Use FILE as a certificate to verify the host\-key or keys.

The certificates are used to establish a chain of trust for the verification of
the host\-key documents. Specify this option twice to specify the IBM Z signing
key and the intermediate CA certificate (signed by the root CA).
.RE
.PP
\-\-crl <FILE>
.RS 4
Use FILE as a certificate revocation list (CRL).

The list is used to check whether a certificate of the chain of trust is
revoked. Specify this option multiple times to use multiple CRLs.
.RE
.PP
\-\-offline
.RS 4
Make no attempt to download CRLs.
.RE
.PP
\-\-root\-ca <ROOT_CA>
.RS 4
Use FILE as the root\-CA certificate for the verification.

If omitted, the system wide\-root CAs installed on the system are used. Use this
only if you trust the specified certificate.
.RE
.PP
\-\-version
.RS 4
Print version information and exit.
.RE
.PP
\-\-hkd\-version <VERSION>
.RS 4
Specify the Host\-key version to use.
[default: 'auto']

Possible values:
.RS 4
\- \fB1\fP: Version 1 \- uses traditional cryptographic keys.

\- \fB2\fP: Version 2 \- uses hybrid (post\-quantum) cryptographic keys.

.RE
.RE
.PP
\-h, \-\-help
.RS 4
Print help (see a summary with \fB\-h\fR).
.RE